# DevMetrics - Phase 1 Backend Architecture

## Project Overview
DevMetrics is an Engineering Contribution Analytics Platform designed to measure and visualize individual and team contributions throughout the software development lifecycle.

Phase 1 focuses on building a scalable MERN backend that supports:
* **Authentication** (JWT Flow, Password Hashing)
* **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)**
* **Project Management**
* **Team Management**
* **Task Management**
* **Contribution Analytics Engine**
* **Reports Generation**
* **Notifications Engine**
* **Activity Logs**

---

## Technology Stack

| Layer | Component | Technology / Library |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Server Environment** | Runtime | Node.js |
| **API Layer** | Web Framework | Express.js |
| **Database** | Database Engine | MongoDB Atlas |
| **ODM Layer** | Database Modeler | Mongoose ODM |
| **Authentication** | Hashing & Token | JWT, bcryptjs |
| **Input Validation** | Request Validation | express-validator |
| **Configuration** | Environment Config | dotenv |
| **Logging (Future)** | Log Management | Winston |

---

## Backend Architecture

```
                 [ Client / React Frontend ]
                              │  (HTTPS / JSON REST API)
                              ▼
                      [ REST API Layer ]
                              │  (Routes Routing & Middlewares)
                              ▼
                    [ Express Controllers ]
                              │  (Request Handling & Extraction)
                              ▼
                      [ Service Layer ]
                              │  (Business & Score Calculations)
                              ▼
                    [ MongoDB Database ]
```

---

## User Roles & Access Scope

* **Admin**: Full database management, team configuration, user management, metrics generation, reports access, and full system configuration.
* **Project Manager**: Create projects and teams, assign leaders/developers, configure workflows, track task progression, and generate reports.
* **Team Lead**: Assign and review tasks within their specific teams, view productivity reports, and manage members.
* **Developer**: Claim/update task status, update effort estimation, and check individual metrics.
* **Tester**: Perform code validation runs, log bug status, and upload coverage/test reports.

